1tlb|v|To disunite; to divide; to disconnect; to sever; to part in any manner. ; To come between; to keep apart by occupying the space between; to lie between; as, the Mediterranean Sea separates Europe and Africa. ; To set apart; to select from among others, as for a special use or service. ; To part; to become disunited; to be disconnected; to withdraw from one another; as, the family separated.	o:on8,60,8;ond,54,7;sjp,53,7;b6s,50,16;1t43,47,62;opy,46,4;43c,39,4;oq5,36,7;9i9,32,4;7ij,31,3~1t43,47,62;1mo2,19,19;b6s,50,16;kq1,25,16;ii9,10,11;21y4,1,10;on8,60,8;20f9,8,8;1xrc,26,8;oq5,36,7	s:24ia,45,230;dsh,4,3;1xjl,3,3~24ia,45,230;dsh,4,3;1xjl,3,3	d:on4,42,41;e9a,36,53;22vi,26,9;d45,17,10~e9a,36,53;on4,42,41;d45,17,10;22vi,26,9	D:1e09,10,6~1e09,10,6
