1tuh|a|of Set ; Fixed in position; immovable; rigid; as, a set line; a set countenance. ; Firm; unchanging; obstinate; as, set opinions or prejudices. ; Regular; uniform; formal; as, a set discourse; a set battle. ; Established; prescribed; as, set forms of prayer. ; Adjusted; arranged; formed; adapted.	j:sma,26,3;8rz,24,3;zo6,10,6;szx,10,1;27pj,8,3;22r3,3,1~zo6,10,6;8rz,24,3;27pj,8,3;sma,26,3;22r3,3,1;szx,10,1	e:29dh,30,3;1krb,13,2;12bs,10,2;im4,3,1;i4,1,1~29dh,30,3;12bs,10,2;1krb,13,2;im4,3,1;i4,1,1
