1tva|n|of Set ; The act of one who, or that which, sets; as, the setting of type, or of gems; the setting of the sun; the setting (hardening) of moist plaster of Paris; the setting (set) of a current. ; The act of marking the position of game, as a setter does; also, hunting with a setter. ; Something set in, or inserted. ; That in which something, as a gem, is set; as, the gold setting of a jeweled pin.	a:1aam,43,2;fdp,41,3;d7l,37,4;b30,35,3;ftg,30,2;125u,27,4;h59,27,4;1p8u,26,1;e1v,26,4;117w,24,3~sx8,9,5;1luk,4,5;n2b,24,5;45o,5,4;d7l,37,4;e1v,26,4;125u,27,4;h59,27,4;117w,24,3;12l4,8,3	v:dye,56,7;dfp,46,2;fdp,25,1~dye,56,7;dfp,46,2;fdp,25,1	V:nyv,25,1;a7s,13,5~a7s,13,5;nyv,25,1	n:1y0t,13,1;v95,9,2;1vby,5,1;1v0x,3,2~v95,9,2;1v0x,3,2;1vby,5,1;1y0t,13,1	N:27if,27,1~27if,27,1
